architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-source-defect-scout.md:10:- Tool/render boundaries: completed guard evidence keeps deleted mutable authorities, duplicate renderers, placeholder tools, and stale e2e contracts absent according to `architecture-audit/final-review/cross-arch-guard-coverage-map.md:12`, `architecture-audit/final-review/cross-arch-guard-coverage-map.md:15`, `architecture-audit/final-review/cross-arch-guard-coverage-map.md:18`, and `architecture-audit/final-review/cross-arch-guard-coverage-map.md:20`.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-source-defect-scout.md:16:- `frontend/src/composables/useSnapping.ts:2` imports `useWorldStore`, and `frontend/src/composables/useSnapping.ts:19` plus `frontend/src/composables/useSnapping.ts:47` fall back to `worldStore.allElements2D[0]?.planeId` when no injected reducer runtime exists. That fallback reintroduces behavior based on a separate projection surface rather than the reducer snapshot authority described in `architecture-audit/final-review/00-summary.md:11`.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-source-defect-scout.md:17:- `frontend/src/composables/useSnapping.ts:94` and `frontend/src/composables/useSnapping.ts:106` cast `Point2D` to `any` to read coordinates, while `frontend/src/composables/useSnapping.ts:97` through `frontend/src/composables/useSnapping.ts:99` and `frontend/src/composables/useSnapping.ts:109` through `frontend/src/composables/useSnapping.ts:111` return `0` for point kinds that require computed geometry. This is a live placeholder geometry path in `frontend/src`, not merely documentation.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-source-defect-scout.md:18:- Usage search found `useSnapping` is not imported by current runtime or tests outside its own file, while `worldStore` is only used by `useSnapping` plus its own store definition; see `.saivage/stages/ci-new-cycle-source-defect-scout/logs/live-usage-query.stdout.log:1`. That makes the island either dead code that should be deleted under the no-backcompat/deletion posture, or an unintegrated feature that must be redesigned around `ProjectStateRecord` selectors before use.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-source-defect-scout.md:20:This does not reopen `ARCH-001` through `ARCH-012` as completed issues. It is a new continuous-improvement candidate because the source evidence is narrower than the original resolved defects: a residual, apparently unused projection/snapping island remains after the final review's broad reducer-authority cleanup.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-source-defect-scout.md:25:Objective: decide and execute one source-grounded deletion-first cleanup for `frontend/src/stores/worldStore.ts` and `frontend/src/composables/useSnapping.ts`; delete both if they are unused, or replace the snapping logic with reducer-selector-backed geometry in the same stage only if a current runtime caller is introduced and justified. No compatibility facade, no dual projection authority, and no placeholder `0` geometry path should remain.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-source-defect-scout.md:29:Acceptance criteria: remove unused `worldStore`/`useSnapping` source and any obsolete tests/types/imports, or land a single reducer-backed snapping implementation with focused tests; add/update a guard so placeholder snapping and duplicate projection-state authority cannot return; run `npm run lint`, focused Vitest for changed files, `npm run build`, `npm run test:post-overhaul-guards`, full `npm test`, and Playwright only if UI behavior is touched; refresh live preview if frontend runtime source changes.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-delete-unused-snapping-worldstore-island.md:10:- `frontend/src/composables/useSnapping.ts:1` deleted the unused snapping composable, including its `worldStore.allElements2D` fallback and placeholder coordinate logic.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-delete-unused-snapping-worldstore-island.md:16:`frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:21` records the deleted paths, `frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:25` through `frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:56` define targeted forbidden imports/usages/patterns, and `frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:648` verifies the deleted files and placeholder snapping island do not return.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-source-defect-scout-after-snapping-cleanup.md:11:- Reducer/domain authority remains centralized in current source. `frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectStateRuntime.ts:15` documents that the holder stores only immutable `ProjectStateRecord` data plus runtime metadata, `frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectStateRuntime.ts:22` keeps the state private, and `frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectStateRuntime.ts:42` commits cloned records through `createProjectStateRecord` before notifying subscribers. No fresh mutable-authority island comparable to the deleted snapping store was found in this bounded pass.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-source-defect-scout-after-snapping-cleanup.md:12:- Persistence/API contracts remain current-snapshot and no-backcompat by code path. `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:1` declares current reducer-state snapshot persistence, `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:31` forbids command-history persistence keys, `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:72` validates schema/provenance/domain before restore, and `backend/src/api/projects.ts:5` through `backend/src/api/projects.ts:27` define the backend schema/contract/forbidden-field boundary. No fresh source signal showed legacy command-stream or projection-array acceptance.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-source-control-archival-plan.md:20:Full tests are not rerun for this documentation-only archival plan because this task only classifies source-control/archive batches from existing path-only evidence and does not modify implementation or test code. If any implementation code changes before archival, rerun the normal acceptance cadence from `package.json:10`.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-source-control-archival-plan.md:75:Before any commit or archive operation, a human reviewer should confirm:
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-source-control-archival-plan.md:90:5. **Package/workspace batch**: `frontend/package.json`, `package-lock.json`, and any reviewed root workspace/package changes.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-source-control-archival-plan.md:91:6. **Deletion batch**: pre-design/spec-pack deletions and deleted legacy command-operation/test surfaces, with a final human deletion review.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-source-control-archival-plan.md:96:2. Run a path-only staging preview before any commit, using the same categories as `.saivage/stages/ci-source-control-archival-plan-2026-05-24/logs/path-only-git-status.stdout.log:1`.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-source-control-archival-plan.md:99:5. After final source/archive selection, rerun the full acceptance cadence if any implementation/test/package content changed after `architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-acceptance-refresh.md:1`.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-004-decision-conformance-refresh.md:4:This continuous-improvement check revalidated current source conformance to the ARCH-004 decision without implementation changes. The decision selected a command-first pointer pipeline where tools translate user input into typed command intents, and rejected direct canvas/world mutation or compatibility shims (`architecture-audit/decisions/ARCH-004.md:10`, `architecture-audit/decisions/ARCH-004.md:18`, `architecture-audit/decisions/ARCH-004.md:22`).
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-004-decision-conformance-refresh.md:11:- `frontend/src/components/workspace/SvgCanvas.vue:727` through `frontend/src/components/workspace/SvgCanvas.vue:747` looks up the active tool, delegates non-select canvas clicks to `ITool.createCommandIntent(...)`, then executes successful intents through `executeToolCommandIntent(...)` instead of mutating a `World`/`ProjectionPlane` authority or old `Workspace2D` path.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-004-decision-conformance-refresh.md:14:- `frontend/tests/unit/tools/pointTool.spec.ts:155` through `frontend/tests/unit/tools/pointTool.spec.ts:177` statically guards the focused suite against imports of deleted legacy pointer/direct-mutation surfaces such as `Workspace2D`, `ElementRenderer`, `World`, `ProjectionPlane`, `ProcessTree`, and `DependencyService`.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-004-decision-conformance-refresh.md:15:- `frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:129` through `frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:135` lists the deleted ARCH-004 legacy canvas surfaces as absent guard targets, and the deleted-surface invariant at `frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:459` through `frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:464` fails if any are restored.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-004-decision-conformance-refresh.md:38:The same log shows `frontend/src/components/workspace/SvgCanvas.vue` as the only direct file in `frontend/src/components/workspace/`, and the safe filename search for the old direct-mutation/legacy authority filenames under `frontend/src` returned no paths.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-005-decision-conformance-refresh.md:13:- `ProjectStateRuntimeHolder` owns the reducer record state and documents that it must not retain mutable geometry, construction-history, dependency-service, or adapter instances (`frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectStateRuntime.ts:14`, `frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectStateRuntime.ts:21`, `frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectStateRuntime.ts:44`).
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-005-decision-conformance-refresh.md:19:`ProjectStateRuntimeSnapshot` still carries runtime metadata named `version`, and `ProjectStateRuntimeHolder` increments it on commit (`frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectStateRuntime.ts:5`, `frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectStateRuntime.ts:22`, `frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectStateRuntime.ts:48`). This is not acting as the deleted ARCH-005 Vue-facing manual refresh authority: the current snapshot composable returns `ProjectStateRecord` only and ignores that metadata (`frontend/src/composables/useProjectStateRuntimeSnapshot.ts:5`, `frontend/src/composables/useProjectStateRuntimeSnapshot.ts:8`), while the panel selectors consume `projectState.value` rather than a version counter (`frontend/src/components/panels/ActionsPanel.vue:45`, `frontend/src/components/panels/ActionsPanel.vue:48`, `frontend/src/components/panels/ActionsPanel.vue:52`).
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-005-decision-conformance-refresh.md:24:- `source-anchors.stdout.log:1` records line-anchored evidence for the decision, runtime holder, Vue snapshot composable, selectors, panel consumer, and focused reactive selector spec.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-005-decision-conformance-refresh.md:25:- `safe-absence-evidence.stdout.log:1` confirms these deleted legacy authority files are absent: `frontend/src/domain/world/World.ts`, `frontend/src/domain/processTree/ProcessTree.ts`, `frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectionPlane.ts`, and `frontend/src/domain/viewState/ProjectionPlane.ts`.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-006-decision-conformance-refresh.md:46:ARCH-006 remains resolved. Current source continues to route rendering through domain-owned typed presentation primitives in `frontend/src/domain/presentation/Paper.ts`, while `frontend/src/components/workspace/SvgCanvas.vue` consumes those primitives rather than reintroducing component-local projection authority or compatibility render adapters. The duplicate renderer services/components remain absent, and both required focused validations passed.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-007-decision-conformance-refresh.md:13:### Typed snapshot contract and arbitrary/legacy payload rejection
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-007-decision-conformance-refresh.md:17:- `backend/src/api/projects.ts:22` through `backend/src/api/projects.ts:31` enumerate deleted legacy command-stream and old element fields; `backend/src/api/projects.ts:226` through `backend/src/api/projects.ts:240` recursively reject those fields anywhere in the submitted payload.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-007-decision-conformance-refresh.md:19:- `backend/src/api/projects.ts:141` through `backend/src/api/projects.ts:195` validate provenance and the reducer `ProjectStateRecordDTO` domain shape, including current projection-plane records and rejection of legacy projection-plane arrays at `backend/src/api/projects.ts:184` through `backend/src/api/projects.ts:193`.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-007-decision-conformance-refresh.md:27:- `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:13` through `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:20` assert the typed error body and explicitly reject legacy `{ error }` aliases.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-007-decision-conformance-refresh.md:39:- `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:22` through `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:62` assert current DTO shape, schema `4.0.0`, `current-snapshot` provenance, reducer projection-plane records, and absence of legacy command/element surfaces.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-007-decision-conformance-refresh.md:42:- `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:208` through `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:351` verify full reducer snapshot replacement and reject partial, arbitrary, schema-mismatched, provenance-mismatched, unknown, and legacy projection-plane payloads.
