architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-002-decision-conformance-refresh.md:31:Backend API validation is likewise strict: it pins `CURRENT_CONTRACT` to `current-snapshot` (`backend/src/api/projects.ts:8`), validates project schema/provenance/domain on replacement (`backend/src/api/projects.ts:106`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:119`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:127`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:141`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:145`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:156`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:160`), rejects legacy projection-plane arrays in the domain (`backend/src/api/projects.ts:187`), and rejects unsupported legacy project fields before acceptance (`backend/src/api/projects.ts:236`). The backend test suite explicitly covers weak create payload rejection (`backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:146`, `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:150`), schema/provenance/domain mismatch rejection (`backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:279`, `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:288`, `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:291`, `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:299`, `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:303`, `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:307`), and command-stream legacy fields without migration aliases (`backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:353`, `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:355`, `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:358`, `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:359`, `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:366`).
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-002-decision-conformance-refresh.md:33:**Classification:** conformant. No compatibility migration reader was found in the inspected persistence paths.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-002-decision-conformance-refresh.md:37:`ProjectService` documentation states that runtime command stacks are intentionally not serialized or restored and that old mutable shapes are rejected (`frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:2`, `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:4`, `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:5`, `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:6`). Its forbidden persistence-field list includes `undoStack` and `redoStack` (`frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:37`, `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:38`), and restore clears the optional runtime `CommandStack` instead of reconstructing undo/redo history from persisted data (`frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:69`, `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:70`, `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:71`, `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:72`).
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-002-decision-conformance-refresh.md:39:`CommandStack` itself remains an in-memory command history object: it holds private `#undoStack` and `#redoStack` arrays (`frontend/src/commands/CommandStack.ts:11`, `frontend/src/commands/CommandStack.ts:12`), mutates them through runtime push/undo/redo/clear operations (`frontend/src/commands/CommandStack.ts:36`, `frontend/src/commands/CommandStack.ts:39`, `frontend/src/commands/CommandStack.ts:51`, `frontend/src/commands/CommandStack.ts:53`, `frontend/src/commands/CommandStack.ts:65`, `frontend/src/commands/CommandStack.ts:67`, `frontend/src/commands/CommandStack.ts:102`, `frontend/src/commands/CommandStack.ts:103`), and exposes only runtime counts/capabilities (`frontend/src/commands/CommandStack.ts:74`, `frontend/src/commands/CommandStack.ts:81`, `frontend/src/commands/CommandStack.ts:88`, `frontend/src/commands/CommandStack.ts:95`). No serialization getter/restoration API is present in the inspected class.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-002-decision-conformance-refresh.md:41:Backend API also treats command-stack fields as legacy/unsupported: `undoStack` and `redoStack` appear in the rejected legacy field list (`backend/src/api/projects.ts:25`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:26`) and unsupported legacy fields throw an invalid payload error (`backend/src/api/projects.ts:236`).
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-002-decision-conformance-refresh.md:47:Frontend round-trip tests assert that serialized project JSON does not contain `undoStack` or `redoStack` (`frontend/tests/unit/services/ProjectService.roundTrip.spec.ts:15`, `frontend/tests/unit/services/ProjectService.roundTrip.spec.ts:16`), that current snapshots carry schema/provenance (`frontend/tests/unit/services/ProjectService.roundTrip.spec.ts:38`, `frontend/tests/unit/services/ProjectService.roundTrip.spec.ts:43`, `frontend/tests/unit/services/ProjectService.roundTrip.spec.ts:44`, `frontend/tests/unit/services/ProjectService.roundTrip.spec.ts:46`), that restore returns the authoritative record and clears runtime command history (`frontend/tests/unit/services/ProjectService.roundTrip.spec.ts:56`), that old command-stream files are rejected (`frontend/tests/unit/services/ProjectService.roundTrip.spec.ts:70`, `frontend/tests/unit/services/ProjectService.roundTrip.spec.ts:80`), and that mutable projection-plane arrays are rejected (`frontend/tests/unit/services/ProjectService.roundTrip.spec.ts:83`, `frontend/tests/unit/services/ProjectService.roundTrip.spec.ts:102`).
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-002-decision-conformance-refresh.md:51:Backend integration tests assert current DTO creation (`backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:129`, `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:137`), full reducer snapshot replacement (`backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:209`, `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:218`, `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:253`), strict legacy/schema/provenance rejection (`backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:279`, `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:288`, `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:291`, `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:299`, `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:303`), and legacy command-stream field rejection without aliases (`backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:353`, `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:355`, `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:358`, `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:359`).
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-002-decision-conformance-refresh.md:68:ARCH-002 remains decision-conformant. The current frontend and backend persistence surfaces use a single current `4.0.0` `ProjectStateRecord` snapshot plus `current-snapshot` provenance DTO, reject weak/legacy/project-command shapes instead of migrating them, and keep `CommandStack` / `undoStack` / `redoStack` internals runtime-only. Required focused, guard, lint, build, and full test validations all passed. No concrete ARCH-002 regression was found, so no runtime source changes were made.
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-003-decision-conformance-refresh.md:10:- The decision forbids compatibility shims, adapters, dual paths, old command aliases, migration readers, and preserved legacy DTOs (`architecture-audit/decisions/ARCH-003.md:20`).
architecture-audit/continuous-improvement/2026-05-24-arch-003-decision-conformance-refresh.md:11:- The plan requires an immutable project-state reducer as the only domain authority with no backward-compatibility adapter, migration reader, old command alias, or dual runtime path (`architecture-audit/plans/ARCH-003.md:15`). It also requires deterministic reducer command/dependency behavior and direct reducer-state persistence (`architecture-audit/plans/ARCH-003.md:64`, `architecture-audit/plans/ARCH-003.md:66`).
