architecture-audit/final-review/11-specs-contracts.md:15:## Residual decision
architecture-audit/final-review/12-documentation.md:7:Current user/developer documentation cites current source: `README.md:1` describes workspace commands and current architecture; `frontend/REALIZATION_ARCHITECTURE.md:1` documents ProjectState-driven realization; `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:1` documents current workspace build/deploy; `docs/GOOGLE_DRIVE_SETUP.md:1` uses synthetic placeholders and current Drive/session references.
architecture-audit/final-review/12-documentation.md:12:## Deletion / no-backcompat check
architecture-audit/final-review/12-documentation.md:13:Historical pre-design files `pre-spec.md`, `pre-plan.md`, `pre-spec-ui.md`, `pre-spec-ui-tool.md`, and the stale `specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/` tree are absent per `.saivage/stages/phase-g-final-review/logs/filesystem-deletion-evidence.log:1`. Live docs do not promise compatibility for deleted formats or old tool/runtime paths.
architecture-audit/final-review/12-documentation.md:15:## Residual decision
architecture-audit/final-review/12-documentation.md:19:The current documentation authority check was optionally hardened in `frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:1` to keep deleted pre-design/spec-pack files absent, reject retained-doc citations that treat deleted historical files as current authority, and scan a narrow selected source/test comment set for stale spec-pack, rejected archival, migration, compatibility-shim, or legacy-preservation language as current behavior. Coverage and validation evidence are summarized in `architecture-audit/final-review/cross-arch-guard-coverage-map.md:1` and `.saivage/stages/ci-arch-012-current-doc-authority-hardening/logs/`; ARCH-012 remains resolved.
architecture-audit/final-review/post-overhaul-guards.md:4:The executable guard in `frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:1` preserves the Phase G acceptance boundary recorded in `architecture-audit/final-review/00-summary.md:1`. It is intentionally narrow: it checks that current reducer snapshot authorities remain present, retained documentation stays anchored to current source/audit paths, deleted legacy paths remain absent, and legacy command-stream persistence is rejected rather than reintroduced through compatibility handling.
architecture-audit/final-review/post-overhaul-guards.md:8:- Retained-documentation authority checks cover `README.md:1`, `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:1`, `docs/GOOGLE_DRIVE_SETUP.md:1`, and `frontend/REALIZATION_ARCHITECTURE.md:1` when present. Each retained document must cite current repository source/audit paths, and any citation to deleted historical pre-design/spec-pack paths must describe those paths as deleted, historical, stale, obsolete, not current, or pre-design rather than current authority.
architecture-audit/final-review/post-overhaul-guards.md:9:- Deleted-surface checks fail if old mutable authorities or stale surfaces are recreated, including `frontend/src/domain/world/World.ts`, `frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectionPlane.ts`, `frontend/src/domain/processTree/ProcessTree.ts`, `frontend/src/services/DependencyService.ts`, `frontend/src/commands/operations/viewState/ViewStateOperations.ts`, old `.old.ts` tools, duplicate renderer services, and historical pre-spec/spec paths such as `pre-spec.md` and `specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/spec.md`.
architecture-audit/final-review/post-overhaul-guards.md:10:- The negative persistence check calls `ProjectService.validateProjectData` from `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:1` with otherwise-current snapshot envelopes containing legacy `commands`, `commandHistory`, `undoStack`, `redoStack`, `SerializedCommand`, or `SerializedOperation` fields. The test must throw instead of accepting or migrating those payloads.
architecture-audit/final-review/post-overhaul-guards.md:14:- The guards reject legacy command-stream and pre-current DTO fields (`commands`, `commandHistory`, `undoStack`, `redoStack`, `SerializedCommand`, `SerializedOperation`, `elements2D`, `elements3D`) at top-level and nested payload positions rather than accepting, migrating, or aliasing them.
architecture-audit/final-review/post-overhaul-guards.md:15:- Malformed `4.0.0`/`current-snapshot` envelopes are covered with missing/extra top-level fields, domain/provenance extra fields, schema mismatches, provenance app/contract/source mismatches, and legacy projection-plane arrays.
architecture-audit/final-review/post-overhaul-guards.md:17:- Invalid current-contract requests assert typed API bodies `{ code, message, status }` and explicitly reject legacy `{ error }` aliases.
architecture-audit/final-review/post-overhaul-guards.md:47:The same guard rejects mutating validation lint behavior for the root, frontend, and backend package scripts by checking `package.json:17`, `frontend/package.json:15`, and `backend/package.json:12` for `--fix`, `--write`, or equivalent formatter-write tokens. This ensures the old frontend-only/mutating validation surface cannot return as a compatibility alias or silent lint side effect.
architecture-audit/final-review/post-overhaul-guards.md:58:The guard derives scan candidates only from tracked repository paths returned by `git ls-files`, filters them to allowed source/docs/test roots, and excludes forbidden or operational paths before any file read. Exclusions include `.saivage/auth-profiles.json`, `.saivage/saivage.json`, any basename beginning with `.env` such as `.envrc` (including nested allowed-root examples), provider config directories, OAuth token stores, shell-history paths, and keychain paths. The test asserts those exclusions with synthetic path samples and proves untracked/out-of-root candidates are not read, logged, grepped, or opened.
architecture-audit/final-review/post-overhaul-guards.md:60:The invariant fails on real-looking credential literals in the allowed scan surface: private key block headers, OAuth access/refresh token forms, Google OAuth client secret forms, `Authorization: Bearer` literals, and API-key assignments or JSON fields. Lines clearly marked as placeholder/example/dummy/fake/test/synthetic/mock/sample/redacted are allowed, and the spec includes in-test fail/allow samples proving both behaviors.
architecture-audit/final-review/post-overhaul-guards.md:65:The post-overhaul invariant guard now includes a static ARCH-011/current e2e contract check in `frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:1`. It scans active `.spec.ts` files under `frontend/tests/e2e` and requires the retained Playwright contract specs `frontend/tests/e2e/current-persistence-contract.spec.ts:1` and `frontend/tests/e2e/current-ui-contract.spec.ts:1` to remain active. The same guard fails if stale pre-overhaul or placeholder/transport spec filenames return, including `persistence.spec.ts`, `undo-redo.spec.ts`, `selection.spec.ts`, `geometry.spec.ts`, and `transport`/`placeholder` spec variants.
architecture-audit/final-review/post-overhaul-guards.md:67:The guard also reads the retained e2e source text rather than launching browser flows from Vitest. For persistence, `frontend/tests/e2e/current-persistence-contract.spec.ts:1` must assert the `ProjectStateRecord`/`current-snapshot` payload shape, current `domain.projectionPlanes` state, absent legacy `commands`/`commandHistory` fields, and HTTP 400 rejection for deleted command-stream payloads. For UI, `frontend/tests/e2e/current-ui-contract.spec.ts:1` must assert current executable tool ids, absence of the deleted transport/placeholder surface, and current app-shell hooks such as `svg-canvas`, `status-bar`, `elements-panel`, `actions-panel`, and `plane-selector`.
architecture-audit/final-review/cross-arch-guard-coverage-map.md:8:| Issue | Decision / proposal outcome | Implementation and final-review evidence | Existing executable guard coverage | Unguarded residual risk |
architecture-audit/final-review/cross-arch-guard-coverage-map.md:11:| ARCH-002 | Resolved by selected Proposal B: replace weak project persistence/command replay with the current reducer snapshot contract; see `architecture-audit/decisions/ARCH-002.md:1` and `architecture-audit/proposals/ARCH-002/proposal-b.md:1`. | Current snapshot DTO and legacy command-stream rejection live in `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:1` and `backend/src/models/Project.ts:1`; final evidence is in `architecture-audit/implementation-log/ARCH-002.md:1` and `architecture-audit/final-review/08-persistence-drive.md:1`. | Frontend guard rejects legacy `commands`, `commandHistory`, `undoStack`, `redoStack`, `SerializedCommand`, and `SerializedOperation` through `ProjectService.validateProjectData` in `frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:551`; backend API/storage tests reject legacy fields in `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:249`. | No unresolved persistence-contract risk. Optional future hardening could add property-based malformed DTO generation, but current no-backcompat contract is guarded. |
architecture-audit/final-review/cross-arch-guard-coverage-map.md:12:| ARCH-003 | Resolved by selected Proposal B, later completed by final mutable-authority deletion; see `architecture-audit/decisions/ARCH-003.md:1`, `architecture-audit/proposals/ARCH-003/proposal-b.md:1`, and the superseding register trace in `architecture-audit/issues/register.md:1`. | Reducer runtime authority is `frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectStateRuntime.ts:1` over records from `frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectState.ts:1`; deleted mutable authorities are cross-checked in `architecture-audit/implementation-log/ARCH-003.md:1` and `architecture-audit/final-review/04-domain-model.md:1`. | Deleted-authority guard keeps `frontend/src/domain/world/World.ts`, `frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectionPlane.ts`, `frontend/src/domain/processTree/ProcessTree.ts`, and `frontend/src/services/DependencyService.ts` absent in `frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:66`; final evidence is summarized in `architecture-audit/final-review/post-overhaul-guards.md:1`. | No unresolved multi-authority risk. Optional future hardening could add reducer-level invariant fuzzing, but the old mutable authority surfaces are executable-deletion guarded. |
architecture-audit/final-review/cross-arch-guard-coverage-map.md:13:| ARCH-004 | Resolved by selected Proposal B: unify canvas/tool interaction around command-intent execution; see `architecture-audit/decisions/ARCH-004.md:1` and `architecture-audit/proposals/ARCH-004/proposal-b.md:1`. | Current boundary is `frontend/src/tools/ITool.ts:1`, `frontend/src/composables/useCommandExecution.ts:1`, and `frontend/src/components/workspace/SvgCanvas.vue:1`; evidence is in `architecture-audit/implementation-log/ARCH-004.md:1` and `architecture-audit/final-review/07-tooling-state-machine.md:1`. | Deletion guard keeps the old parallel canvas/render path absent, including `frontend/src/components/workspace/Workspace2D.vue` and `frontend/src/components/workspace/ElementRenderer.vue`, via `frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:66`; current e2e UI contract is required by `frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:426` and implemented in `frontend/tests/e2e/current-ui-contract.spec.ts:1`. | No unresolved split-interaction risk. Fine-grained pointer-sequence behavioral regressions remain outside this static guard and are optional future UI test hardening. |
architecture-audit/final-review/cross-arch-guard-coverage-map.md:14:| ARCH-005 | Resolved by selected Proposal A: move process-tree/reactive reads to ProjectState snapshots instead of polling/version forcing; see `architecture-audit/decisions/ARCH-005.md:1` and `architecture-audit/proposals/ARCH-005/proposal-a.md:1`. | Snapshot reactivity is in `frontend/src/composables/useProjectStateRuntimeSnapshot.ts:1` and process UI reads in `frontend/src/components/panels/ActionsPanel.vue:1`; evidence is in `architecture-audit/implementation-log/ARCH-005.md:1` and `architecture-audit/final-review/03-frontend-layering.md:1`. | `frontend/tests/unit/domain/projectStateRuntimeReactiveSelectors.spec.ts:1` now mounts a Vue computed-selector probe over `ProjectStateRuntimeHolder` and `useProjectStateRuntimeSnapshot`, proving process/action and element read models update after runtime commit, reset, and replacement. `frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:66` also keeps deleted mutable `frontend/src/domain/processTree/ProcessTree.ts` authority absent. | No unresolved polling-authority risk. This optional reactive selector hardening keeps ARCH-005 resolved and adds a focused regression guard against stale snapshot-derived UI/process reads. |
architecture-audit/final-review/cross-arch-guard-coverage-map.md:16:| ARCH-007 | Resolved by selected Proposal A: enforce typed backend DTO/API/storage contracts and safe IDs; see `architecture-audit/decisions/ARCH-007.md:1` and `architecture-audit/proposals/ARCH-007/proposal-a.md:1`. | Typed API and storage contracts are `backend/src/api/projects.ts:1`, `backend/src/storage/FileStorage.ts:1`, and `backend/src/storage/ProjectRepository.ts:1`; evidence is in `architecture-audit/implementation-log/ARCH-007.md:1` and `architecture-audit/final-review/02-backend-layering.md:1`. | `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:105` through `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:332` guard typed errors, current DTO replacement, legacy field rejection, and path confinement. The backend guard is part of `npm run test:post-overhaul-guards` in `package.json:18`. | No unresolved backend contract risk. Optional future hardening could add concurrency/storage-failure cases, but arbitrary update/path traversal defects are guarded. |
architecture-audit/final-review/cross-arch-guard-coverage-map.md:17:| ARCH-008 | Resolved by selected Proposal B as adjusted by direct stage implementation: process provenance is reducer-authored and authoritative; see `architecture-audit/decisions/ARCH-008.md:1`, `architecture-audit/proposals/ARCH-008/proposal-b.md:1`, and `architecture-audit/implementation-log/ARCH-008.md:1`. | Current provenance writes are in `frontend/src/commands/operations/OperationReducers.ts:1` and read models in `frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectStateProcessReducers.ts:1`; final evidence is in `architecture-audit/final-review/04-domain-model.md:1`. | Guard coverage is indirect through current reducer-authority checks in `frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:15` and deleted mutable process-tree authority absence in `frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:66`; final-review evidence remains the primary ARCH-008 guard. | No unresolved process-tree-authority risk. Optional future hardening could add reducer provenance assertions per operation type, but the old non-authoritative ProcessTree surface is absent. |
architecture-audit/final-review/cross-arch-guard-coverage-map.md:18:| ARCH-009 | Resolved by selected Proposal B: delete placeholder/legacy tools and keep palette entries executable; see `architecture-audit/decisions/ARCH-009.md:1` and `architecture-audit/proposals/ARCH-009/proposal-b.md:1`. | Runtime palette configuration is `frontend/src/components/toolbars/mainToolbarTools.ts:1` and `frontend/src/config/toolFamilies.ts:1`; deletion evidence is in `architecture-audit/implementation-log/ARCH-009.md:1` and `architecture-audit/final-review/07-tooling-state-machine.md:1`. | `frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:66` guard keeps `.old.ts` tools and `frontend/src/components/icons/toolbar/TransportPointIcon.vue` absent; `frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:426` checks active e2e source excludes transport/placeholder behavior via `frontend/tests/e2e/current-ui-contract.spec.ts:1`. | No unresolved placeholder-tool risk. Optional future hardening could assert every toolbar ID has an executable command-intent integration test. |
architecture-audit/final-review/cross-arch-guard-coverage-map.md:19:| ARCH-010 | Resolved by selected Proposal A: extract App shell responsibilities into Drive/session/keyboard/canvas composables; see `architecture-audit/decisions/ARCH-010.md:1` and `architecture-audit/proposals/ARCH-010/proposal-a.md:1`. | Current extraction is visible in `frontend/src/App.vue:1`, `frontend/src/composables/useDriveProjectSession.ts:1`, `frontend/src/composables/useAppKeyboardShortcuts.ts:1`, and `frontend/src/composables/useAppCanvasSession.ts:1`; evidence is in `architecture-audit/implementation-log/ARCH-010.md:1` and `architecture-audit/final-review/03-frontend-layering.md:1`. | `frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:1` now includes a focused static ARCH-010 guard requiring App.vue to compose through `useDriveProjectSession`, `useAppKeyboardShortcuts`, and `useAppCanvasSession`, rejecting reintroduced App-owned localStorage restoration, Drive singleton/private-access orchestration, inline autosave, keyboard listener, and canvas/session orchestration. The same guard checks the three composables own their intended current concerns without old localStorage compatibility, command/store keyboard authority, or Drive/persistence canvas coupling. | No unresolved App-shell risk. This optional hardening adds executable import/source-boundary checks while keeping ARCH-010 resolved. |
architecture-audit/final-review/cross-arch-guard-coverage-map.md:20:| ARCH-011 | Resolved by selected Proposal A: make test and contract coverage include frontend, backend, and current e2e contracts; see `architecture-audit/decisions/ARCH-011.md:1` and `architecture-audit/proposals/ARCH-011/proposal-a.md:1`. | Root full test command is `package.json:15`; backend integration coverage is `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:1`; active current e2e specs are `frontend/tests/e2e/current-persistence-contract.spec.ts:1` and `frontend/tests/e2e/current-ui-contract.spec.ts:1`; evidence is in `architecture-audit/implementation-log/ARCH-011.md:1` and `architecture-audit/final-review/09-test-surface.md:1`. | `frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:426` requires current e2e specs to remain active and stale `persistence.spec.ts`, `undo-redo.spec.ts`, `selection.spec.ts`, `geometry.spec.ts`, transport, and placeholder specs to remain absent. Backend API/storage tests are run by `npm run test:post-overhaul-guards` from `package.json:18`. | No unresolved test-surface risk. Optional future hardening could broaden scenario coverage, but stale pre-overhaul test contracts are guarded. |
architecture-audit/final-review/cross-arch-guard-coverage-map.md:28:All twelve ARCH issues remain **resolved** by the current issue register and Phase G final review (`architecture-audit/issues/register.md:1`, `architecture-audit/final-review/00-summary.md:1`). The residual items above are optional future hardening ideas only; they are not reopened issues because the current source and guard evidence do not expose a concrete architecture defect.
architecture-audit/final-review/cross-arch-guard-coverage-map.md:37:A focused reducer invariant guard was added in `frontend/tests/unit/domain/projectStateReducerProvenanceInvariants.spec.ts:1` for the current `ProjectStateRecord` authority in `frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectState.ts:1`, reducer runtime boundary in `frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectStateRuntime.ts:1`, process reducer read helpers in `frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectStateProcessReducers.ts:1`, and construction reducer writes in `frontend/src/commands/operations/OperationReducers.ts:1`. The guard covers free point construction plus dependent line, segment, circle, and guide construction through current operation APIs only. It asserts frozen plain DTO state, deterministic action ids/createdAt/root child order/process-tree version, and dependency graph input-to-output/input-to-action/action-to-output edges. This is optional hardening for resolved ARCH-003, ARCH-005, and ARCH-008 coverage; it does not reopen any ARCH issue. Focused validation evidence is recorded in `.saivage/stages/ci-domain-reducer-provenance-invariant-hardening/logs/focused-projectstate-reducer-invariants.stdout.log:1`.
architecture-audit/final-review/cross-arch-guard-coverage-map.md:40:Focused pointer/tool command-intent coverage was added in `frontend/tests/unit/tools/pointTool.spec.ts:1` for representative `PointTool` and `LineTool` flows through the current `frontend/src/composables/useCommandExecution.ts:1` and `frontend/src/commands/CommandStack.ts:1` boundary. The guard also checks this focused suite does not import deleted legacy direct-mutation/canvas surfaces such as `Workspace2D`, `ElementRenderer`, `World`, `ProjectionPlane`, `ProcessTree`, or `DependencyService`. This is optional hardening for resolved ARCH-004 only; the issue remains resolved by `architecture-audit/issues/register.md:1` and is not reopened. Validation evidence for this hardening is recorded under `.saivage/stages/ci-arch-004-command-intent-pointer-hardening/logs/`, including the focused pointer test, post-overhaul guards, lint, build, full test, Playwright/e2e attempt, and live preview reachability logs.
architecture-audit/final-review/cross-arch-guard-coverage-map.md:44:A focused reactive selector guard was added in `frontend/tests/unit/domain/projectStateRuntimeReactiveSelectors.spec.ts:1` for the current runtime holder in `frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectStateRuntime.ts:1`, Vue snapshot composable in `frontend/src/composables/useProjectStateRuntimeSnapshot.ts:1`, and selector read models in `frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectStateSelectors.ts:1`. The test mounts a small Vue computed probe and verifies ProjectState process/action and element panel-equivalent read models update from runtime `commit`, `reset`, and replacement commits without polling, force-refresh helpers, manual version counters as the assertion mechanism, command invalidation facts, or deleted mutable authorities. ARCH-005 remains resolved by `architecture-audit/issues/register.md:1`; this is optional hardening only. Validation evidence for this stage is recorded under `.saivage/stages/ci-arch-005-reactive-selector-hardening/logs/`.
architecture-audit/final-review/cross-arch-guard-coverage-map.md:50:Focused backend API/storage guard coverage was strengthened in `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:1` for the current typed project route contract in `backend/src/api/projects.ts:1`, project-local filename guard in `backend/src/storage/FileStorage.ts:1`, and strict project id namespace in `backend/src/storage/ProjectRepository.ts:1`. The added cases reject non-object, array, null, extra-key, arbitrary blob, and malformed nested DTO update payloads with `{ code, message, status }` only, assert no legacy `{ error }` alias appears, and verify list metadata skips invalid project filenames/malformed JSON without leaking `domain` or `provenance`. ARCH-007 remains resolved by `architecture-audit/issues/register.md:1`; this is optional hardening only, with no compatibility reader, migration path, old DTO alias, or broad validation framework introduced. Validation evidence is recorded under `.saivage/stages/ci-arch-007-backend-error-storage-hardening/logs/`.
architecture-audit/final-review/cross-arch-guard-coverage-map.md:56:Focused runtime palette coverage was added in `frontend/tests/unit/config.toolFamilies.spec.ts:1` for the current toolbar authority `frontend/src/components/toolbars/mainToolbarTools.ts:1`, grouped palette config `frontend/src/config/toolFamilies.ts:1`, current `ToolType` union in `frontend/src/stores/toolStore.ts:1`, and current `ITool` command-intent implementations under `frontend/src/tools/`. The guard asserts `MAIN_TOOLBAR_TOOLS` and `TOOL_FAMILIES` expose only select plus implemented command-intent construction tools, instantiates each current tool class to verify the registered id matches the implementation API, keeps deleted `.old.ts` tool files absent, and rejects transport, placeholder, roadmap, future, planned, documentation-only, and placeholder-icon runtime registrations. ARCH-009 remains resolved by `architecture-audit/issues/register.md:1`; this is optional hardening only and does not add executable manifests for unsupported tools. Focused validation evidence is recorded in `.saivage/stages/ci-arch-009-runtime-tool-palette-hardening/logs/focused-arch-009-palette-guard.stdout.log:1`.
architecture-audit/final-review/cross-arch-guard-coverage-map.md:60:Focused static App-shell boundary coverage was added in `frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:1` for the current shell in `frontend/src/App.vue:1`, Drive/session lifecycle in `frontend/src/composables/useDriveProjectSession.ts:1`, keyboard action router in `frontend/src/composables/useAppKeyboardShortcuts.ts:1`, and canvas/session boundary in `frontend/src/composables/useAppCanvasSession.ts:1`. The guard fails if App.vue reintroduces deleted `diedrico_last_file`/`localStorage` restoration, direct `new GoogleDriveService` orchestration, private Drive access, inline autosave timers/subscriptions, inline keydown listener orchestration, or canvas/session implementation details beyond handler wiring. It also asserts the Drive composable owns GoogleDriveService/ProjectService/autosave concerns without localStorage compatibility, the keyboard composable remains an injected-action router without command/store authority, and the canvas composable owns active-plane/coordinate/fit/cascade-preview concerns without Drive/project persistence coupling. ARCH-010 remains resolved by `architecture-audit/issues/register.md:1`; this is optional hardening only. Focused validation evidence is recorded in `.saivage/stages/ci-arch-010-app-shell-boundary-hardening/logs/focused-arch-010-guard-rerun.stdout.log:1`.
architecture-audit/final-review/cross-arch-guard-coverage-map.md:63:Focused ARCH-011 guard coverage was strengthened in `frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:1` so the root `package.json:15` `test` script and `package.json:18` `test:post-overhaul-guards` command must continue wiring the frontend architecture guard and backend `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:1` contract tests. The guard also requires the current ProjectService contract specs in `frontend/tests/unit/services/ProjectService.roundTrip.spec.ts:1` and `frontend/tests/unit/services/ProjectService.selfContainment.spec.ts:1`, current Playwright contracts in `frontend/tests/e2e/current-persistence-contract.spec.ts:1` and `frontend/tests/e2e/current-ui-contract.spec.ts:1`, and absence of stale spec-only contracts under `specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/contracts`. ARCH-011 remains resolved by `architecture-audit/issues/register.md:1`; this is optional hardening only, with no generated contract toolchain, compatibility reader, migration shim, or broad acceptance-suite framework. Validation evidence for this stage is recorded under `.saivage/stages/ci-arch-011-contract-coverage-hardening/logs/`.
architecture-audit/final-review/cross-arch-guard-coverage-map.md:66:Focused ARCH-012 guard coverage was strengthened in `frontend/tests/unit/architecture/postOverhaulInvariants.spec.ts:1` for retained current docs (`README.md:1`, `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:1`, `docs/GOOGLE_DRIVE_SETUP.md:1`, `frontend/REALIZATION_ARCHITECTURE.md:1`) and a bounded source/test comment set around validation, persistence, tooling, and rendering behavior. The guard continues to keep deleted historical/pre-design artifacts such as `pre-spec.md`, `pre-plan.md`, `pre-spec-ui.md`, `pre-spec-ui-tool.md`, and `specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/` absent; it also fails if retained docs cite those deleted artifacts as current authority or if selected source/test comments present stale spec-pack, rejected archival, migration, compatibility-shim, or legacy-preservation language as current behavior. ARCH-012 remains resolved by `architecture-audit/issues/register.md:1`; this is optional hardening only. Validation evidence for this stage is recorded under `.saivage/stages/ci-arch-012-current-doc-authority-hardening/logs/`.
